==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm}} ''hemlok, hemeluc'', from {{etyl|ang}} ''hymlīc(e)'' 'hemlock, bryony, convulvus', literally 'hops-like', from {{term|hymele|lang=ang}} 'hop-vine', from {{proto|Germanic|xumalaz||xumalōn}} (cf. {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|humall|lang=non}}, {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|homele|lang=gml}}), from Sarmato-Scythian *''haumala'' (cf. [[Ossetian]] ''xumællæg'' 'hops'), diminutive of *''hauma'' 'ephedra; juice' (compare {{etyl|ae|-}} ''haoma'', [[Baluchi]] ''hum'', {{etyl|fa|-}} {{term|hōm}}), from {{proto|Indo-Iranian|sauma}} (compare [[Sanskrit]] ''soma''), from {{proto|Indo-European|seue-}} 'to suck; juice'. More at [[suck]].

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# Any of several [[poisonous]] [[umbellifer]]ous [[plant]]s, of the genera ''[[Conium]]'' and ''[[Cicuta]]''; the [[poison]] obtained from these plants
# Any of several [[coniferous]] [[tree]]s, of the genus ''[[Tsuga]]'', that grow in [[North America]]; the [[wood]] of such trees

